# Hy4-flash's placed prompt pass (hy4pass: R1 the Select cache as rooms with the server's K/V floor 8,192 / spill, R2 the
# common PlacedSide batch half, R3 the placed pass) against the 0.3.15 binary, whose placed load feeds a prompt one id a
# step. The effect [derived, specs/day1117/hy4/hy4pp-report.md §2.2-2.3]: a step re-reads a layer's 463 host experts a
# token (31.5 GB a layer for 512 ids, the host leg 24.5-25.9 ms of a token's 31.5 ms); the pass reads each once a 512-row
# unit and runs it at m = 16 columns, the host union 51-66 ms a layer and unit at 111-142 us an expert (V4.1's union law
# scaled by the MAC ratio): pp512 182-235 at the 0.3.15 plan, 219-284 with R1's floor plan (card experts 2,004 -> ~5,400).
# Decode at depth 512: 28.2 -> 32.5-33.5 tok/s from the floor plan [derived]; 0.3.15 measured 31.71.
kind: ab
question: does the placed prompt pass lift Hy4-flash's prompt on one RTX 5090 by the bulk the derivation gives?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 512, prose corpus, one RTX 5090 32 GB, the serving defaults - (hy4pass - 0.3.15) / 0.3.15, paired
  by round
unit: %
predict: +475..+795
rounds: 2
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, two binaries' per-round pp ratios; the effect is two orders above it
condition: BLOOMERY_MODEL=hy_v4_flash just depth-serve bloomery-rel0315@portable:512 bloomery-hy4pass:512 and their
  :4096 arms, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2, the order rotated every round, one fresh server an arm, the file warm in the page cache
decide-in: land R1-R3 into 0.3.15 and re-table Hy4's row from the release sitting
decide-below: read PromptStats (host serve against card time) to find the term that is wrong before landing
decide-above: refit the host union's a and c to Hy4's 1536-wide experts and redo the stream table (§2.4)
